This paper examines the normalized ground state solution for the given biharmonic Choquard type equation \begin{align*}
  \begin{split}
  \left\{
  \begin{array}{ll}
  \Delta^2u-\beta\Delta u=\lambda u+\left(\frac{1}{|x|^\mu}\ast u^p\right)~\mbox{in}~\mathbb{R}^4,
  \end{array}
  \right.
  \end{split}
  \displaystyle{\lim_{|x|\to\infty}|\nabla u(x)|=0}
  \end{align*} under specific constraints and parameters. The normalized ground state solution is defined as the solution that minimizes the functional \begin{align*}
